  "items": [
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "The Israeli military says that they killed Ra'ad Sa'ad, a senior Hamas military commander, in an apparent violation of the ceasefire. ((The Times of Israel))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Israeli Defence Forces issue an evacuation order in southern Lebanese villages in preparation for planned airstrikes on Hezbollah targets. ((The Jerusalem Post))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "An attacker identified by the United States Central Command as a member of ISIL opens fire on a joint Syrian and American convoy in Palmyra, killing two US service members and one American civilian interpreter and injuring three others, before being killed by return fire. ((SANA via Al Jazeera))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "A Rapid Support Forces (RSF) drone strike kills at least three people in El-Obeid, North Kordofan, Sudan. ((Al Jazeera))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "An RSF drone strike on a United Nations base in Kadugli, South Kordofan, Sudan, kills six Bangladeshi peacekeepers and injures eight others. ((Al Jazeera))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "In response to resumed clashes with Thailand, Cambodia shuts down border crossings. ((BBC News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "United States president Donald Trump says a new ceasefire has been brokered. However, hours later, Thai leaders announce an increased commitment to fighting Cambodian forces. ((France 24))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "At least two people are killed, and eight others are injured in a mass shooting at Brown University in Providence, Rhode Island, United States. The suspect fled the scene and is not in custody. ((NBC News)) ((BNO News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "Belarus releases 123 political prisoners, including Nobel Peace prize laureate Ales Bialiatski and protest leader Maria Kalesnikava, from prisons after the United States lifts its sanctions. ((BBC))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "Spanish authorities dismantle a drug-trafficking network that uses helicopters to transport large quantities of hashish from Morocco into southern Spain, arresting six suspects in a joint operation involving several European countries. ((AFP via Arab News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "Munich police arrest five men, including three Moroccans, one Egyptian, and one Syrian of allegedly planning to attack a Christmas market in Dingolfing, Bavaria, Germany. ((DW))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "The M23 states that it has captured several hundred Burundian soldiers during its recent offensive in eastern Democratic Republic of the Congo, including around Uvira. ((Reuters))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "The Israeli military kills Ra'ad Sa'ad, a senior Hamas military commander, in an airstrike against a vehicle in Gaza City, in an apparent violation of the ceasefire. Four other people were also killed in the attack, and 25 more injured. ((The Times of Israel)) ((Al Jazeera))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "In response to resumed clashes with Thailand, Cambodia shuts down its border crossings with Thailand. ((BBC News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "Nine African migrants are killed from freezing temperatures near the Algeria–Morocco border. ((MSN))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "Eight people are killed after a multicab falls into a terrain in Ayungon, Negros Oriental, Philippines. ((The Philippine Star))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "Two people are killed and nine others are injured in a mass shooting at Brown University in Providence, Rhode Island, United States. The suspect fled the scene and is not in custody. ((NBC News)) ((BNO News))"
    },
    {
